          "explanation": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>Let $A$ = scratch resistance high, $B$ = shock resistance high. $P(A)=\\dfrac{144+22}{200}=\\dfrac{166}{200}$, $P(B)=\\dfrac{144+25}{200}=\\dfrac{169}{200}$, $P(A \\cap B)=\\dfrac{144}{200}$. By the addition rule, $P(A \\cup B)=\\dfrac{166+169-144}{200}=\\dfrac{191}{200}=0.955$. Equivalently, the only cell excluded is low/low: $1-\\dfrac{9}{200}=0.955$.</p></div><div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>Đặt $A$ = chống trầy cao, $B$ = chống sốc cao. $P(A)=\\dfrac{166}{200}$, $P(B)=\\dfrac{169}{200}$, $P(A \\cap B)=\\dfrac{144}{200}$. Theo quy tắc cộng, $P(A \\cup B)=\\dfrac{166+169-144}{200}=\\dfrac{191}{200}=0{,}955$. Cách khác: ô duy nhất bị loại là thấp/thấp, nên $1-\\dfrac{9}{200}=0{,}955$.</p></div>"
